# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — ProcessQueue duplicate-offset parity
# Recorded: 2026-10-23 00:23:07 UTC
# Code revision: 8bf6ee40

## Compatibility finding

Pinned Java 5.5.1 stores ready messages in `msgTreeMap` and orderly in-flight
messages in a separate `consumingMsgOrderlyTreeMap`. `putMessage` can therefore
add another ready message at an offset that is still in flight. The ready copy
increments count and size; `commit` removes the in-flight entry and keeps the
ready copy, `rollback` overwrites the ready copy without changing the counters,
and `removeMessage` removes only the ready copy. Replacing an already-ready
offset does not update `queueOffsetMax` or its cached body size.

Rust now retains a ready duplicate beside its in-flight message and includes
that entry in the public message-tree view, cache span, queue info, and batch
completion paths. The invoked Java facade fixture checks duplicate insert,
commit, rollback, removal, counters, message body and offset bookkeeping. An
internal batch regression verifies that terminal completion leaves the
repulled message ready. Fixture SHA-256:
`f4c918d58b0fd0104511281b8380a13356cd0dfb5bd1d2d370fe9b890e32bb31`.

